For some time ago I was asking if anybody had had problems with hack.font
under 2.04. I didn't get a clear answer, so I decided to take a closer
look myself (OK, OK, should have done it before the first posting).

Well - SnoopDos showed that nethack tries to open 'Nethack:Nethack:hack.font'
which naturally fails. I don't know where this odd path comes from - maybe
I've got a screwed .cnf file or something... In any case it worked under 1.3.
I found a simple, inelegant workaround for this problem: the trick is to
load the hack.font into memory before launching nethack, so that it doesn't
need to be seeked from the disk.

So, if you have had problems with hack.font, you might want to try this:

	1. Copy file 'hack.font' and dir 'hack' from your nethack:
	   directory to your fonts: directory.

	2. Add line 'setfont hack.font 8' into your s:User-Startup.
	   This sets your bootup window to use hack.font and as a
	   side-effect leaves it in memory.

	3. Start nethack normally.


Remember: don't try to fix something that isn't broken! If you can see
the custom characters in the game (walls, doors etc.) your hack.font
probably works fine and you should be happy as ever.


